{
  "slug": "pitch-deck-writing",
  "concept": "Pitch Deck Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "A pitch deck is a slide-based artifact that compresses a fundraising, sales, or partnership case into a tight narrative arc — usually 10 to 14 slides — designed to be skimmed in minutes and remembered",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A pitch deck is a slide-based artifact that compresses a fundraising, sales, or partnership case into a tight narrative arc - usually 10 to 14 slides - designed to be skimmed in minutes and remembered in seconds.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The 10/20/30 rule (Kawasaki)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Guy Kawasaki's rule for investor/pitch contexts:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#1-the-102030-rule-kawasaki",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "10 slides - the human mind cannot absorb more than ten concepts in a single sitting in a pitch context",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#1-the-102030-rule-kawasaki",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "20 minutes - even if you have a full hour, present in 20 minutes; leave the rest for discussion",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#1-the-102030-rule-kawasaki",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "30-point minimum font - if you cannot fit your message in 30pt type, you have too many words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#1-the-102030-rule-kawasaki",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. The canonical Sequoia / Reid Hoffman structure",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "10–12 slides in this order:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Title / Company purpose - one-line description",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Problem - the customer pain, with evidence",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution - your product as the answer",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Why now - timing argument; why this couldn't have been built 5 years ago",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Market size - TAM/SAM/SOM, bottom-up preferred",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Competition - who else is in the space, how you differ",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Product - screenshots, demo, key features",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Business model - how you make money",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Team - why this team can win",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Traction - what you've already proven",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Financials - current state and projections",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask - how much you're raising, what you'll do with it",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Slide 4 (\"Why now\") is the slide most founders skip and the slide most VCs care about.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#2-the-canonical-sequoia-reid-hoffman-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. The narrative arc — problem → solution → traction → team → ask",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Strip away the template specifics and every effective pitch deck follows five beats:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#3-the-narrative-arc-problem-solution-traction-team-ask",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Problem - establish the pain. The reader nods.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#3-the-narrative-arc-problem-solution-traction-team-ask",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Solution - show your answer. The reader believes the answer is plausible.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#3-the-narrative-arc-problem-solution-traction-team-ask",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Traction - prove it's working. The reader believes the answer is real.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#3-the-narrative-arc-problem-solution-traction-team-ask",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Team - prove you can execute. The reader believes you specifically can win.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#3-the-narrative-arc-problem-solution-traction-team-ask",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask - close. The reader knows what you want and what they get.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#3-the-narrative-arc-problem-solution-traction-team-ask",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. The appendix convention",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Strong decks have an appendix - 5 to 20 extra slides beyond the main 10–12 - NOT shown in the live pitch but sent with the deck.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#4-the-appendix-convention",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. The \"no cliffhanger\" rule",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Pitch decks are NOT mystery novels. Slide 1 should already answer \"what does this company do\" at headline level.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#5-the-no-cliffhanger-rule",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. \"What I most want you to remember\" — the closer",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "End the deck with one slide that names the single thing you want the audience to walk away remembering. Not a recap - one sentence, one number, one image.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#6-what-i-most-want-you-to-remember-the-closer",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. The slide-title-as-thesis rule",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every slide has a title. The title is a thesis, not a category.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#7-the-slide-title-as-thesis-rule",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Category title (weak): \"Market Size\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#7-the-slide-title-as-thesis-rule",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Thesis title (strong): \"$47B TAM growing 22% annually; we serve the underserved bottom 60%\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#7-the-slide-title-as-thesis-rule",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The mystery opening - first 3 slides don't say what the company does.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Wall-of-text slides - paragraphs of body copy presented live.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No \"why now\" - deck skips the timing argument.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No traction (when you have some) - burying real data deep.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Generic team slide - \"20+ years experience\" instead of specific credentials.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Competition denial - \"we have no competitors.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "TAM inflation - \"$2T global market\" with no bottom-up math.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "No ask - the deck ends with vague \"let's talk.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Cliffhanger close - last slide is \"Thank you\" or \"Questions?\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/pitch-deck-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
